<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Disposition flow redesign, 2026-08-19. POST-destructive deletions.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit
    go-ahead. This file only DESCRIBES deletions; it performs nothing on its own.

    DELETES EXACTLY TWO COMPONENTS.

    1. ValidationRule Disposition__c.Wire_Complete_Before_Completed
       Superseded by Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes, which is the SAME rule pointed
       at the renamed terminal stage. A validation-rule API-name change is a delete
       plus a create, not a rename, so both files exist for one deploy.
       POST-destructive is load-bearing: the replacement must be live BEFORE the old
       rule goes, or there is a window with no wire gate at all.
       ⚠ IT MUST NOT BE LEFT BEHIND. It names the picklist value 'Completed', and a
       validation rule referencing a value blocks that value's manual deletion in
       Setup, which is the final step of this programme.

    2. PathAssistant Disposition_Path
       The legacy, INACTIVE __MASTER__ path. It was kept as the record of the guidance
       text the two record-typed paths copied forward. That justification has expired:
       both paths were REBUILT on 2026-08-19 and no longer carry its text, and its four
       remaining steps name Call for Offers and Completed, two of the three retired
       values. Like the rule above, a path assistant step referencing a picklist value
       blocks that value's deletion in Setup.
       ⚠ recordTypeName is NOT updateable, so this path can never be repointed; deletion
       is the only route. Its content is recoverable from git history.

    EXPLICITLY NOT IN SCOPE:
      - Disposition_Path_On_Market / Disposition_Path_Off_Market: REBUILT, must survive.
      - All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression: MODIFIED in place, no API-name change.
      - The three retired PICKLIST VALUES (Call for Offers, Disposition Offer, Completed):
        A DEPLOY CANNOT DELETE A PICKLIST VALUE. They are deleted BY HAND in Setup after
        this runs. Do not try to add them here.

    HOW TO RUN IT (only once authorised, and only AFTER the main payload has landed):
      run `sf project deploy start` with
        the manifest flag           pointing at this folder's package.xml
        the post destructive flag   pointing at this file
        the target org flag         set to the disposition org alias
        the test level flag         set to RunLocalTests, and a 30 minute wait.
      The flag prefixes are spelled out in words on purpose: an XML comment body cannot
      contain two consecutive hyphens, so writing the real flags here would make this
      file unparseable.

    Rollback: both components are recoverable from git history and can be redeployed.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>Disposition__c.Wire_Complete_Before_Completed</members>
        <name>ValidationRule</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Disposition_Path</members>
        <name>PathAssistant</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
